</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-39e68f4627e03b8a907b0391c1ac7e50be204fe870e0cb0d44a29654e4f44e3b">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/3/40/020" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">3.40.020 Definitions.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p><span>As used in this Chapter, the following definitions apply:</span></p><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A. &nbsp;ABC </strong>means any board, commission, committee or similar group that provides an opportunity for appointed community members to participate in the City's governance or decision-making process. This does not include groups that do not report or make recommendations to the City.</span></li><li><span><strong>B. Enabling legislation</strong> means the Charter provision, ballot measure act, City ordinance or Code provision that establishes the ABC, its duties and authority.</span></li><li><span><strong>C. &nbsp;Creating authority </strong>means the Council or the Mayor. Under Charter Section 2-103, the Council has authority to establish boards and commissions, while the Mayor has authority to establish advisory boards and advisory commissions.</span></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-c55dae01bdbb36b5a7c1f975eac35e61738676377b64ab009bf07b95f0c966ce">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-4df53f6099700d1cb126922af8ed6a7ae2a45e49450c9cefb3c96d9b38d774d2">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/3/40/030" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">3.40.030 Classification.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p><span>As used in this Chapter, ABCs fall into two classes, each with sub-classes defined here:</span></p><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>ABCs the Mayor or Council does not have sole authority to create, alter, or dissolve:</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp; Independent Charter body</strong> means an ABC created by provision of the City Charter.</span></li><li><span><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp; Ballot measure oversight body</strong> means an ABC created by voter approval of a ballot measure that reviews and oversees implementation of the program funded by the ballot measure. If the oversight body is in Portland City Code, then Council could later amend the City Code to alter the oversight body.</span></li><li><span><strong>3.&nbsp;&nbsp; Body required by law</strong> means an ABC that fulfills functions required by state or federal law, including by state or federal statute, code or court order. This includes quasi-judicial bodies such as hearings or appeals boards. The term also includes bodies that advise the quasi-judicial bodies or the Council, fulfill state requirements in areas such as land use or transportation planning, or perform duties required by federal law.</span></li><li><span><strong>4.&nbsp;&nbsp; Intergovernmental body</strong> means an ABC created under an intergovernmental agreement that provides advice and guidance according to the terms of the agreement.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>B.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>ABCs the Mayor or Council has sole authority to create, alter, or dissolve:</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp; Ongoing advisory body</strong> means an ABC that offers recommendations but that has no independent authority to make decisions on behalf of the City on policy or administration.</span></li><li><span><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp; Limited advisory body</strong> means an ABC established for a specific and time-limited advisory purpose and that is intended to terminate after completion of its assigned duties or a certain period of time.</span></li><li><span><strong>3. Council-delegated decision-making body </strong>means an ABC established by Council and granted specific, delegated authority to make decisions on behalf of the City.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>C.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>ABCs do not include:</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Bodies comprised solely of City employees;</span></li><li><span><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Informal community sounding boards or consultations not appointed by the City; or</span></li><li><span><strong>3.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Intergovernmental bodies where the City has only elected representation.</span></li></ol></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-428c88135d4f656336935e2fba60020361a0efa4f132dc66f38bd0ef3dde8709">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-14dc377dc2874a00eb9d21ba17cd5b43f955a08fe878ad9ac7b78f2218a8bfa3">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/3/40/040" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">3.40.040 Application of Chapter.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A.</strong> The requirements of this Chapter apply only to the following ABCs:</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Independent Charter bodies;</span></li><li><span><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Ballot measure oversight bodies;</span></li><li><span><strong>3.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Bodies required by law;</span></li><li><span><strong>4.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Bodies created by the Council, whatever their classification;</span></li><li><span><strong>5.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Ongoing advisory bodies; and</span></li><li><span><strong>6.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Limited advisory bodies.</span></li></ol></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-b261e1bc613315d8a22be19763b003c153e2467083c35760eebf4d3bb98f79d0">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-48a256dbcd3b1095f31d1f81ce794526bc958b9d9d68731adca1513e04d9c0ca">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/3/40/050" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">3.40.050 ABC Creation, Sunset and Periodic Review.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><ol class="code-list"><li><span><strong>A.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Creation of ABCs.</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The Council and the Mayor have the authority to create, alter or abolish ABCs as provided under Charter Section 2-103.</span></li><li><span><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The Mayor may create, alter, or abolish advisory ABCs through independent executive action at the Mayor's sole discretion as provided in Charter Section 2-103.</span></li><li><span><strong>3.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The Council will create new ABCs through ordinance with the exception that the Council may create limited advisory bodies through resolution.</span></li><li><span><strong>4.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The Mayor or a Councilor may propose the creation of an ABC by Council under Subsection 3.40.050 A.3. and will be referred to as the ABC's sponsor.&nbsp; An ABC may be created under Subsection 3.40.050 A.3. only after the sponsor has analyzed and reported on:</span><ol><li><span><strong>a.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The proposed ABC's primary purpose, mission, functions and responsibilities;</span></li><li><span><strong>b.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The number of seats on the ABC, qualifications for the seats, if any, and the appointing authority for each seat;</span></li><li><span><strong>c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Any possible duplication of efforts or conflicts with existing ABCs; and</span></li><li><span><strong>d.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The anticipated financial, staffing, and operational impacts upon City resources and whether the ABC will have dedicated resources.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>5.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Each ABC will have only the functions, powers, duties, and responsibilities specifically delegated to it by the creating authority through enabling legislation or resolution or through Mayoral action, as appropriate. The Council may, at any time, by majority vote, modify the functions, powers, duties, and responsibilities of an ABC created by ordinance or resolution. The Mayor may, at any time, modify the functions, powers, duties, and responsibilities of an ABC created by Mayoral action.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>B.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Sunset. An ABC will sunset and be automatically dissolved after four years of operation unless:</span><ol><li><span><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The creating authority extends the ABC's term; or</span></li><li><span><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The ABC's enabling legislation or resolution, or Mayoral action, as appropriate, specifies a different sunset.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>C.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; Reporting of ABCs. For all ABCs not created by Council, the City Administrator shall submit the following information to Council within 30 days of the ABC's establishment or abolition:</span><ol><li><span><strong>1. </strong>All information listed under Subsection 3.40.050 A.4.;</span></li><li><span><strong>2. </strong>The ABC's sunset date or renewal term, if applicable; and</span></li><li><span><strong>3.&nbsp;</strong>A copy of adopted bylaws, if any, must be provided within 30 days of adoption.</span></li></ol></li><li><span><strong>D. </strong>Membership of ABCs, including names, qualifications, organizational affiliations, and appointment terms will be listed where other information about ABCs is publicly available. For ABCs not confirmed by Council, the City Administrator will inform Council of membership information within 30 days of any appointment(s).</span></li><li><span><strong>E.</strong> Periodic review. The City Administrator will report to Council periodically about the status of all ABCs. The report should assess whether existing ABCs: are inactive or outdated; might be combined with other ABCs with similar purpose, duties or functions; fulfill an ongoing purpose or could be time-limited with a sunset applied; and align with citywide ABC standards and practices.</span></li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-31f01d2419eefe55b6c3fbee00121ac9d2cd92c83e1b122c77ca0d52efbf1477">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-04eec60cffaa7c260b3ed571e6c3b2d6460879be042e56f1cc2e6979517d5d5c">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>

    </div>
          <div class="views-row">
           
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h3>
        <a href="/code/3/40/060" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">3.40.060 ABC Member Conduct.</span>
</a>
    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p><span>Members of ABCs are public officials subject to rules of conduct established by the Bureau of Human Resources, including rules covering ethical standards, and workplace harassment, discrimination and retaliation. The Bureau of Human Resources is responsible for enforcing those rules.</span></p></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-f155a686d28b1781988e604674707ae5571f0c8adc2d82d34baeeade6511f8b6">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
